  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Sunday...\n\nA wave moving across northern Montana will drop a mostly dry cold\nfront through the region this morning into this afternoon. There \nwill be two pushes with this system, with an initial frontal \npassage occurring this morning. Then, pressure rises spread \nacross the area into the afternoon, bringing an additional push of\nwinds. Winds will be breezy out of the north with each push, with\nwidespread gusts of 20 to 40 mph. Isolated showers and\nweak thunderstorms are possible (10-30% chance) near the Dakota \nborder late this afternoon into this evening behind the second \npush. Otherwise, any precipitation will be mainly limited to the \nmountains and foothills.\n\nHighs today will be in the mid 70s to mid 80s, around 10 to 20\ndegrees above normal. Given the very warm temperatures and dry and\nbreezy conditions, a Red Flag Warning is in effect from 9 AM to 9\nPM today for portions of Treasure, Rosebud, Custer, Fallon, and \nCarter Counties. Within the warning, the main concerns for \nelevated to critical fire weather conditions exist along and north\nof Interstate 94 and US Highway 12.\n\nTuesday into Wednesday will see continued very warm and dry \nconditions under an upper level ridge. Highs on Tuesday will \ngenerally be in the 70s before increasing to 80s to low 90s \nWednesday. Winds on Wednesday may be breezy out of the south, \nwith gusts of 15 to 35 mph.\n\nLate Wednesday/early Thursday, models have come into better\nagreement for a trough to move through the region, followed by\nadditional shortwaves into the weekend. There is a widespread \n30-60% chance of showers and thunderstorms Thursday afternoon and\na 20-40% chance each day through Sunday. Temperatures will cool\nslightly, falling from low 70s to low 80s Thursday to mostly 60s\nby Sunday. Archer",
